* [Stacks Project, Tag 02RW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02RW)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits TopologicalSpace

universe u

namespace Stacks.Chow

/-! ### The zero scheme of a section of a finite locally free module -/

/-- **The zero scheme of a global section, for a module of any rank.** This is the standing
construction of the section [Stacks, Tag 0FA8]: the closed subscheme of `X` whose quasi-coherent
sheaf of ideals is the image of `s : ℰ^∨ ⟶ 𝒪_X`, written on an affine open `U` as the ideal
generated by the values `φ (s|_U)` of the `Γ(X, U)`-linear functionals `φ` on `Γ(ℰ, U)`.

For an invertible module this is the zero scheme of [Stacks, Tag 02OQ],
`Stacks.Divisors.zeroScheme`; see `Stacks.Chow.zeroSchemeOfSection_eq_zeroScheme`. -/
def zeroSchemeOfSection (X : Scheme.{u}) (E : X.Modules) (s : Γ(E, ⊤)) : X.IdealSheafData :=
  Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdeals (fun U =>
    Ideal.span {a : Γ(X, U.1) | ∃ φ : Γ(E, U.1) →ₗ[Γ(X, U.1)] Γ(X, U.1),
      a = φ (E.presheaf.map (homOfLE le_top).op s)})

/-- For an invertible module the zero scheme of a section is the one of [Stacks, Tag 02OQ]: the
two ideal sheaves are given by the same formula, the invertibility playing no part in it. -/
theorem zeroSchemeOfSection_eq_zeroScheme (X : Scheme.{u}) (L : X.Modules)
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj X.ringCatSheaf.property L]
    (s : Γ(L, ⊤)) :
    zeroSchemeOfSection X L s = Stacks.Divisors.zeroScheme X L s :=
  rfl

/-! ### The hypotheses of Stacks 0FA9 -/

/-- **The regular-sequence hypothesis of [Stacks, Tag 0FA9].** For every generic point `ξ` of
the zero scheme `Z(s)` at which the relative dimension over the base is `m`, the ideal that
`Z(s)` cuts out in the local ring `𝒪_{X', ξ}` is generated by a regular sequence of length `r`.

The ideal cut out in the local ring is the kernel of the stalk map of the closed immersion
`Z(s) ⟶ X'`; this is `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.stalkIdeal` written out. -/
def IsRegularZeroSchemeSequence (C : ChowSituation.{u}) {X' : Scheme.{u}} (q : X' ⟶ C.S)
    [LocallyOfFiniteType q] (E : X'.Modules) (s : Γ(E, ⊤)) (r : ℕ) (m : ℤ) : Prop :=
  ∀ ξ : genericPoints (zeroSchemeOfSection X' E s).subscheme,
    relativeDimension C.dimensionFunction q ((zeroSchemeOfSection X' E s).subschemeι ξ.1) = m →
      ∃ rs : List (X'.presheaf.stalk ((zeroSchemeOfSection X' E s).subschemeι ξ.1)),
        rs.length = r ∧
        RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular
          (X'.presheaf.stalk ((zeroSchemeOfSection X' E s).subschemeι ξ.1)) rs ∧
        Ideal.span {a | a ∈ rs} =
          RingHom.ker ((zeroSchemeOfSection X' E s).subschemeι.stalkMap ξ.1).hom

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 0FA9] in the reduced case `X = X'`**, the case the source reduces to with
Stacks 0B7H: with the three hypotheses `dim_δ(X') = n`, `dim_δ(Z(s)) ≤ n - r` and the
regular-sequence condition at the generic points of `Z(s)` of `δ`-dimension `n - r`, the cap
product with the `r`-th Chern class of a module `F` of constant rank `r` on `X'` carries the
fundamental cycle `[X']_n` to `[Z(s)]_{n - r}`.

The source proves this by induction on `r`, the case `r = 1` being Stacks 02SQ and the step
`r > 1` needing the projective space bundle formula of Stacks 02TX, which is not carried in this
repository; see the implementation notes of this file. -/
def TopChernCapEqZeroScheme (C : ChowSituation.{u}) {X' : Scheme.{u}} (q : X' ⟶ C.S)
    [LocallyOfFiniteType q] (r : ℕ) (cap : HigherChernCapRule C r) (F : X'.Modules)
    (hF : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} F r)
    (s : Γ(F, ⊤)) (n : ℤ) : Prop :=
  letI : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} F r := hF
  schemeDeltaDimension C q = (n : EInt) →
  schemeDeltaDimension C ((zeroSchemeOfSection X' F s).subschemeι ≫ q) ≤
      ((n - (r : ℤ) : ℤ) : EInt) →
  IsRegularZeroSchemeSequence C q F s r (n - (r : ℤ)) →
  cap q F n (Fin.last r)
      (QuotientAddGroup.mk' (rationalEquivalences C q n)
        (cycleAssociatedToClosedSubscheme C q (𝟙 X') n)) =
    QuotientAddGroup.mk' (rationalEquivalences C q (n - (r : ℤ)))
      (cycleAssociatedToClosedSubscheme C q
        (zeroSchemeOfSection X' F s).subschemeι (n - (r : ℤ)))

/-! ### Stacks 0FA9 -/

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 0FA9].** Let `(S, δ)` be the base situation of chapter 42, let `X` be locally
of finite type over `S`, let `ℰ` be a finite locally free `𝒪_X`-module of constant rank `r`, let
`f : X' ⟶ X` be locally of finite type and let `s ∈ Γ(X', f^*ℰ)`. Assume `dim_δ(X') = n`, that
`dim_δ(Z(s)) ≤ n - r`, and that for every generic point `ξ ∈ Z(s)` with `δ(ξ) = n - r` the ideal
of `Z(s)` in `𝒪_{X', ξ}` is generated by a regular sequence of length `r`. Then

  `c_r(ℰ) ∩ [X']_n = [Z(s)]_{n - r}`  in  `CH_{n - r}(X')`,

where `c_r(ℰ)` is read as a bivariant class `c` for `𝟙 X` satisfying the characterization
`Stacks.Chow.IsChernClassBivariant` of Stacks 0B7H, and its cap product against the Chow group of
`X'` is transported from `X ×_X X'` to `X'` along the base-change isomorphism, as the defining
conditions of a bivariant class require.

This is the source's statement together with the first step of its proof: the reduction to the
case `X = X'` using that `c_r(ℰ)` is a bivariant class. The reduced case
`Stacks.Chow.TopChernCapEqZeroScheme` is the hypothesis `hreduced`; the source proves it by
induction on `r` from Stacks 02SQ and the projective space bundle formula of Stacks 02TX, and
the latter is not carried in this repository. -/
@[stacks 0FA9 "The statement is the source's in full: all four of its hypotheses are present
and none is weakened. What is supplied unconditionally is the first step of the source's proof,
the reduction to the case `X = X'`: the cap operation of a bivariant class satisfying the
characterization of Tag 0B7H is identified, after transport along the base-change isomorphism,
with the cap product formed on the test scheme with the pulled-back module. The reduced case
itself is carried as the declared hypothesis `hreduced`; the source obtains it by induction on
`r`, whose base case `r = 1` is Tag 02SQ -- proved here as
`Stacks.ChernCap42.firstChernClassCapOfInvertible_closedSubscheme_eq_zeroScheme` -- and whose
step `r > 1` needs the projective space bundle formula of Tag 02TX, the decomposition of
`CH_*(P)` making flat pullback along the projection injective. Only the flatness and
relative-dimension clauses of Tag 02TX are carried in this repository, so that formula is not
available and the rest of this directory carries it as a hypothesis wherever it is needed. The
cap product with the higher Chern classes is the parameter `Stacks.Chow.HigherChernCapRule`
standing in for Tag 0B7G, which is not formalized, as in every other file of this directory. The
